chapter.v:
	A bishop 

	 then must be blameless, the husband of one wife, temperate, sober-minded, of good behavior, hospitable, able to teach;
 [Deut. 33:2;]

	not given 

	 to wine, not violent, not greedy for money, but gentle, not quarrelsome, not covetous;
 [Heb. 10:28]

	(for if 

	 a man does not know how to rule his own house, how will he take care of the church of God?);
 [[2 Pet. 3:13]]

	These things 

	 I write to you, though I hope to come to you shortly;
 [Col. 2:15] [John 1:14]
